---
<SiteLayout
  title="Custom website previews"
  description="Website Support Studio creates custom website previews and provides ongoing website support for local service businesses."
  path="/"
  type="home"
  siteConfigOverride={landingSiteConfig}
>
  <section class="wss-hero" id="custom-preview">
    <div class="wss-hero__content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Website Support Studio</p>
      <h1>Get a free custom website preview for your business.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Send us your current website. We will create a custom homepage preview for your real business so you can see
        what your next website could look like before you spend a dollar.
      </p>
      <div class="wss-actions">
        <a class="button" href="#custom-preview-form">Request your free preview</a>
      </div>
      <div class="wss-proof-strip" aria-label="Preview strengths">
        {proofPoints.map((point) => <span>{point}</span>)}
      </div>
    </div>

    <form class="hero-card wss-request-form wss-hero-form" id="custom-preview-form" novalidate>
      <p class="hero-card-kicker">free custom website preview</p>
      <h2>Request a preview for your business</h2>
      <p>We will review your current site and create a homepage concept built around your actual services and buyers. No payment required to see the preview.</p>
      <p class="hero-form-note">Most website preview requests are delivered within 2-3 business days.</p>
      <label>Website URL<input name="website" type="url" required autocomplete="url" placeholder="https://example.com" /></label>
      <label>Business Type<input name="business-type" type="text" required placeholder="Roofing, HVAC, plumbing, salon..." /></label>
      <label>Email Address<input name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com" /></label>
      <label>Optional challenge<textarea name="challenge" placeholder="What is not working well enough right now?"></textarea></label>
      <button class="button button--green" type="submit">Get My Free Preview</button>
      <p id="wss-reimagine-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="hero-form-status"></p>
    </form>
  </section>

  <section class="wss-how" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="wss-section-top">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2>A simple way to see the direction before you approve the build.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The preview gives you something concrete to judge with your team. If it feels right, we can turn it into a full website and support it after launch.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="wss-step-grid">
      {howItWorks.map((item) => (
        <article class="wss-step-card">
          <span>{item.step}</span>
          <h3>{item.title}</h3>
          <p>{item.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wss-transformations" id="transformations">
    <div class="wss-section-top">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Before and after</p>
        <h2>Side-by-side transformations make the improvement visible.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The preview is not decoration. It shows how an outdated page can become easier to understand, trust, and contact.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="wss-transformation-grid">
      {transformations.map((item) => (
        <article class="wss-transformation-card">
          <p class="wss-transformation-type">{item.businessType}</p>
          <div class="wss-before-after-mockups">
            <div class="wss-before-mockup">
              <p class="wss-transformation-label">Before</p>
              <h3>{item.beforeTitle}</h3>
              <div class="wss-old-site-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
              <ul>
                {item.before.map((point) => <li>{point}</li>)}
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="wss-after-mockup">
              <p class="wss-transformation-label wss-transformation-label--after">After</p>
              <h3>{item.afterTitle}</h3>
              <div class="wss-new-site-layout" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
              <ul>
                {item.after.map((point) => <li>{point}</li>)}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          <strong>{item.outcome}</strong>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wss-gallery-section" id="preview-inspiration">
    <div class="wss-section-top">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Preview inspiration</p>
        <h2>Industry gallery for breadth, relevance, and ideas.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The gallery stays broad on purpose. It shows the industries Website Support Studio can understand, while your preview is still shaped around your real business, service mix, and customer questions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="wss-filter-row" aria-label="Preview focus areas">
      {previewFocusAreas.map((category) => <span>{category}</span>)}
    </div>

    <div class="wss-template-grid wss-industry-grid">
      {previewConcepts.map((concept) => (
        <article class="wss-template-card wss-industry-card">
          <div class="wss-industry-image">
            <img
              src={concept.image}
              srcset={`${concept.image.replace("w=900", "w=480")} 480w, ${concept.image} 900w, ${concept.image.replace("w=900", "w=1200")} 1200w`}
              sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 31vw, (min-width: 768px) 46vw, 92vw"
              alt={`${concept.businessType} website preview concept`}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              width="900"
              height="600"
            />
            <div class="wss-industry-overlay">
              <p>{concept.businessType}</p>
              <strong>{concept.title}</strong>
              <em>{concept.tag}</em>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="wss-template-copy">
            <div>
              <p>{concept.businessType}</p>
              <h3>{concept.title}</h3>
            </div>
            <span>{concept.tag}</span>
          </div>
          <p class="wss-template-outcome">{concept.outcome}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wss-trust-section" id="website-support-trust">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Website support experience</p>
      <h2>Practical website help from preview through improvement.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="wss-trust-list">
      {trustPoints.map((point) => <p>{point}</p>)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wss-comparison">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">After the preview</p>
      <h2>If the direction is right, we can build it and support it.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Website Support Studio creates custom preview concepts, builds practical websites, and provides ongoing support
        so the site keeps working after launch.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="wss-score-grid">
      <article>
        <strong>1</strong>
        <span>custom homepage preview</span>
      </article>
      <article>
        <strong>4</strong>
        <span>simple review steps</span>
      </article>
      <article>
        <strong>0</strong>
        <span>dollars spent before seeing direction</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const form = document.getElementById("custom-preview-form");
      const status = document.getElementById("wss-reimagine-status");
      if (!(form instanceof HTMLFormElement) || !(status instanceof HTMLElement)) return;

      // TODO: connect this submit hook to an email + CRM route later.
      form.addEventListener("submit", (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        status.textContent = "";

        if (!form.checkValidity()) {
          status.textContent = "Please complete the website, business type, and email fields.";
          return;
        }

        const data = {
          website: (form.querySelector('input[name="website"]').value || "").trim(),
          businessType: (form.querySelector('input[name="business-type"]').value || "").trim(),
          email: (form.querySelector('input[name="email"]').value || "").trim(),
          challenge: (form.querySelector('textarea[name="challenge"]').value || "").trim()
        };

        console.log("WSS custom preview request payload (TODO wire-up):", data);
        status.textContent = "Thanks. Your custom preview request is queued for review.";
        form.reset();
      });
    })();
  </script>
</SiteLayout>
